{"type":"message","id":"21108a1f","parentId":"ef56b559","timestamp":"2026-03-08T22:17:26.341Z","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[Sun 2026-03-08 23:13 GMT+1] You are an expert AI systems architect.\n\n**Context:**\n- OpenClaw integrating neuro-memory-agent with evolution\n- Current best thinking: event-mesh connection (continuous), adaptive evolution triggers\n- Need to validate this is the right architecture\n\n**Question:** What could go wrong? Identify failure modes and edge cases.\n\nAnalyze:\n- Python crashes (what happens to event processing?)\n- Memory leaks (neuro-memory storing too much)\n- Conflicting patterns (neuro-memory says X, template says Y)\n- Cold start (no historical data yet)\n- Slow queries (evolution timeout)\n- Data corruption (SQLite corruption)\n- Version mismatch (neuro-memory schema changes)\n\nFor each:\n- Likelihood (low/medium/high)\n- Impact (what breaks)\n- Detection (how to notice)\n- Mitigation (how to prevent/recover)\n\nGive me:\n- Prioritized list (most critical first)\n- Recommended safeguards\n- Graceful degradation strategy\n\nBe specific and opinionated."}],"timestamp":1773008246340}}
{"type":"message","id":"6c114532","parentId":"21108a1f","timestamp":"2026-03-08T22:18:54.022Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"This is a subagent task asking me to analyze failure modes for the OpenClaw + neuro-memory-agent + evolution integration. I need to provide a thorough risk analysis with prioritized failure modes, detection strategies, and mitigation approaches.\n\nLet me think through each scenario systematically:\n\n1. **Python crashes** - If the Python-based neuro-memory-agent crashes, event processing stops\n2. **Memory leaks** - Unbounded growth in neuro-memory storage\n3. **Conflicting patterns** - Disagreement between learned patterns and hardcoded templates\n4. **Cold start** - No historical data for the system to learn from\n5. **Slow queries** - Evolution timing out waiting for neuro-memory responses\n6. **Data corruption** - SQLite database corruption\n7. **Version mismatch** - Schema incompatibility between versions\n\nI should be specific, opinionated, and prioritize by real-world impact. Let me structure this as a comprehensive analysis.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"# Failure Mode Analysis: OpenClaw + Neuro-Memory + Evolution\n\n## 🔴 CRITICAL (Immediate Action Required)\n\n### 1. Python Crashes / Event Processing Death\n\n**Likelihood:** MEDIUM (Python processes do crash, especially with native extensions)  \n**Impact:** CATASTROPHIC - Entire event mesh stops, no predictions, evolution stalls\n\n**What breaks:**\n- Event queue backs up indefinitely\n- No predictions delivered\n- Evolution cycle hangs waiting for neuro-memory responses\n- Cascading failure: downstream systems waiting on predictions timeout\n\n**Detection:**\n- Process health checks (heartbeat/ping)\n- Event queue depth monitoring\n- Last-processed-timestamp watchdog (alert if > 5min stale)\n- TypeScript side: timeout on neuro-memory RPC calls\n\n**Mitigation:**\n```typescript\n// CRITICAL: Implement this pattern\nclass NeuroMemoryClient {\n  private healthCheck = setInterval(() => {\n    if (Date.now() - this.lastResponse > 30000) {\n      this.restartPythonProcess();\n    }\n  }, 10000);\n  \n  async query(pattern: string): Promise<Result> {\n    const timeout = setTimeout(() => {\n      throw new Error('Neuro-memory timeout - falling back to templates');\n    }, 5000);\n    // ... with try/catch fallback to template-based predictions\n  }\n}\n```\n\n**Recovery:** Automatic process restart + event queue replay from last checkpoint\n\n---\n\n### 2. Conflicting Patterns (Neuro vs Template)\n\n**Likelihood:** HIGH (this *will* happen constantly as system learns)  \n**Impact:** MEDIUM-HIGH - Inconsistent behavior, user confusion, wrong predictions\n\n**Scenarios:**\n- Neuro-memory learns users check email at 9am, template says 8am\n- Template: \"weekdays only\", neuro-memory: \"user worked last 3 Saturdays\"\n- Neuro-memory overfits to recent anomaly, template has long-term wisdom\n\n**Detection:**\n- Log confidence scores from both sources\n- Alert when disagreement > threshold (e.g., both >70% confident, opposite predictions)\n- Track prediction accuracy: which source was right?\n\n**Mitigation (opinionated approach):**\n```typescript\nfunction resolvePrediction(neuro: Prediction, template: Prediction): Prediction {\n  // Rule 1: Templates win on safety-critical decisions\n  if (template.safetyCritical) return template;\n  \n  // Rule 2: Neuro wins if confidence > 90% AND recent data (last 7 days)\n  if (neuro.confidence > 0.9 && neuro.dataFreshness < 7) return neuro;\n  \n  // Rule 3: Template wins if neuro data is stale (> 30 days)\n  if (neuro.dataFreshness > 30) return template;\n  \n  // Rule 4: Average/blend for medium confidence\n  return mergePredictions(neuro, template, { \n    weights: [neuro.sampleCount, template.historicalAccuracy] \n  });\n}\n```\n\n**Key insight:** Don't treat this as a bug - it's a feature. Build explicit conflict resolution, not \"hope they agree.\"\n\n---\n\n## 🟡 HIGH (Address Soon)\n\n### 3. Cold Start (No Historical Data)\n\n**Likelihood:** CERTAIN (every new user, every fresh install)  \n**Impact:** MEDIUM - Poor predictions initially, but recoverable\n\n**What breaks:**\n- Neuro-memory returns empty/low-confidence results\n- Evolution has no patterns to optimize\n- Users see generic/template-only behavior\n\n**Detection:**\n- Explicit state: `neuroMemory.isWarmedUp()` → false for first N events\n- Track prediction confidence: average < 50% = cold start mode\n\n**Mitigation:**\n```typescript\n// Graceful degradation strategy\nclass PredictionEngine {\n  get mode(): 'cold-start' | 'warming' | 'normal' {\n    if (this.eventCount < 100) return 'cold-start';\n    if (this.avgConfidence < 0.6) return 'warming';\n    return 'normal';\n  }\n  \n  predict(context: Context): Prediction {\n    if (this.mode === 'cold-start') {\n      // Boost template usage, suppress neuro-memory noise\n      return this.templateOnly(context);\n    }\n    // Gradual blend: 0% neuro at start, 100% at 500 events\n    const neuroWeight = Math.min(this.eventCount / 500, 1);\n    return this.blend(context, { neuroWeight });\n  }\n}\n```\n\n**Recovery time:** ~100-500 events for basic patterns, ~1000+ for sophisticated predictions\n\n---\n\n### 4. Slow Queries / Evolution Timeout\n\n**Likelihood:** MEDIUM (grows with data size)  \n**Impact:** MEDIUM - Evolution cycle fails, but system continues\n\n**What breaks:**\n- Evolution cycle times out waiting for neuro-memory analysis\n- Adaptive triggers don't fire\n- System falls back to static behavior\n\n**Root causes:**\n- SQLite query without index on timestamp column\n- Neuro-memory doing full table scans\n- Python GIL blocking during heavy computation\n- Network latency (if neuro-memory is remote)\n\n**Detection:**\n- Log query durations, alert on p95 > 2s\n- Evolution cycle metrics: success rate, avg duration\n- Track \"timeout fallback\" rate\n\n**Mitigation:**\n```python\n# In neuro-memory-agent, CRITICAL indexes\nCREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_events_timestamp ON events(timestamp);\nCREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_events_type ON events(event_type);\nCREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_events_user ON events(user_id, timestamp DESC);\n\n# Query with explicit limit\ndef get_recent_patterns(user_id: str, limit: int = 1000) -> List[Pattern]:\n    return db.query(\"\"\"\n        SELECT * FROM events \n        WHERE user_id = ? \n        ORDER BY timestamp DESC \n        LIMIT ?\n    \"\"\", [user_id, limit])\n```\n\n**Graceful degradation:**\n```typescript\nclass EvolutionCycle {\n  async run(): Promise<void> {\n    const neuroAnalysis = await Promise.race([\n      this.neuroMemory.analyze(),\n      this.timeout(5000, () => this.fallbackAnalysis())\n    ]);\n    // Continue with partial/templated analysis rather than failing\n  }\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## 🟢 MEDIUM (Plan For)\n\n### 5. Memory Leaks (Unbounded Growth)\n\n**Likelihood:** MEDIUM (classic problem without explicit pruning)  \n**Impact:** MEDIUM - System slows over time, eventually crashes\n\n**What breaks:**\n- SQLite file grows to GBs (disk space)\n- Query times increase linearly/exponentially\n- Python process memory balloons\n- Eventually: OOM kill or disk full\n\n**Detection:**\n- Monitor SQLite file size daily\n- Track Python process RSS memory\n- Alert on > 1GB database or > 500MB process memory\n\n**Mitigation:**\n```python\n# Automatic pruning in neuro-memory-agent\nRETENTION_POLICY = {\n    'raw_events': 30,      # days - keep detailed events for 30 days\n    'daily_summaries': 365, # days - keep aggregates for 1 year\n    'learned_patterns': -1  # forever - but recompute periodically\n}\n\ndef prune_old_data():\n    db.execute(\"\"\"\n        DELETE FROM events \n        WHERE timestamp < datetime('now', ?)\n    \"\"\", [f\"-{RETENTION_POLICY['raw_events']} days\"])\n    \n    # Vacuum monthly to reclaim space\n    if datetime.now().day == 1:\n        db.execute(\"VACUUM\")\n```\n\n**Opinion:** Don't try to keep everything. Aggressive summarization is your friend.\n\n---\n\n### 6. SQLite Data Corruption\n\n**Likelihood:** LOW (SQLite is robust, but not invincible)  \n**Impact:** HIGH - Data loss, potential system halt\n\n**Root causes:**\n- Hard shutdown during write (power loss, kill -9)\n- Disk errors\n- Concurrent write without WAL mode\n- Python crash mid-transaction\n\n**Detection:**\n- SQLite integrity check on startup: `PRAGMA integrity_check`\n- Checksum validation of critical tables\n- Sudden empty/missing tables\n\n**Mitigation:**\n```python\n# Enable WAL mode (Write-Ahead Logging) - CRITICAL\nconn = sqlite3.connect('neuro_memory.db')\nconn.execute('PRAGMA journal_mode=WAL')  # Better concurrency, safer\nconn.execute('PRAGMA synchronous=FULL')  # Maximum durability\n\n# Regular integrity checks\ndef startup_health_check():\n    result = conn.execute(\"PRAGMA integrity_check\").fetchone()\n    if result[0] != 'ok':\n        alert(\"SQLite corruption detected!\")\n        restore_from_backup()\n```\n\n**Backup strategy:**\n```bash\n# Daily backup (sqlite3 tool handles consistency)\nsqlite3 neuro_memory.db \".backup 'backups/neuro_memory_$(date +%Y%m%d).db'\"\n\n# Keep 7 daily + 4 weekly backups\n```\n\n**Recovery:** Restore from backup + replay recent events from event-mesh log (if available)\n\n---\n\n### 7. Version Mismatch (Schema Changes)\n\n**Likelihood:** MEDIUM (happens on updates)  \n**Impact:** MEDIUM - Migration fails or corrupts data\n\n**Scenarios:**\n- Neuro-memory schema v2, OpenClaw expects v1\n- Rolling update: old and new versions running simultaneously\n- Migration script fails halfway\n\n**Detection:**\n- Schema version check on connect\n- `SELECT value FROM metadata WHERE key = 'schema_version'`\n- Mismatch → refuse to start with clear error\n\n**Mitigation:**\n```python\nSCHEMA_VERSION = 3\n\ndef migrate_schema(db, from_version: int):\n    if from_version < 2:\n        db.execute(\"ALTER TABLE events ADD COLUMN confidence REAL\")\n    if from_version < 3:\n        db.execute(\"CREATE INDEX idx_events_confidence ON events(confidence)\")\n    db.execute(\"UPDATE metadata SET value = ? WHERE key = 'schema_version'\", [SCHEMA_VERSION])\n\n# On startup\ncurrent = db.execute(\"SELECT value FROM metadata WHERE key = 'schema_version'\").fetchone()\nif current[0] != SCHEMA_VERSION:\n    if current[0] < SCHEMA_VERSION:\n        migrate_schema(db, current[0])\n    else:\n        raise IncompatibleVersionError(\"Database is newer than code - upgrade OpenClaw\")\n```\n\n**Deployment rule:** Always migrate forward, never run old code on new DB.\n\n---\n\n## 📋 Prioritized Safeguards (Implementation Order)\n\n### Tier 1: Do This Week\n1. **Process health monitoring** - Restart on crash, alert on zombie state\n2. **Timeout on all neuro-memory calls** - 5s default, fallback to templates\n3. **SQLite WAL mode** - Single line, prevents most corruption\n4. **Conflict resolution logic** - Explicit rules for neuro vs template\n\n### Tier 2: Do This Month\n5. **Cold start mode** - Explicit gradual rollout of neuro predictions\n6. **Query performance indexes** - timestamp, user_id, event_type\n7. **Daily backups** - Automated with 7-day retention\n\n### Tier 3: Do This Quarter\n8. **Data pruning** - 30-day raw events, 1-year summaries\n9. **Schema migration system** - Version checks + auto-migrate\n10. **Metrics/dashboards** - Track health, accuracy, performance\n\n---\n\n## 🎯 Graceful Degradation Strategy (The Philosophy)\n\n**Core principle:** The system should *always* function, even if neuro-memory is completely dead.\n\n```typescript\nclass OpenClawCore {\n  // Layers of functionality, each can operate independently\n  predict(context: Context): Prediction {\n    // Layer 1: Always works (hardcoded templates)\n    const base = this.templateEngine.predict(context);\n    \n    // Layer 2: Enhancement (neuro-memory) - optional\n    try {\n      const neuro = await this.neuroMemory.query(context);\n      return this.merge(base, neuro);\n    } catch (e) {\n      // Neuro failed? Return template prediction\n      logger.warn('Neuro-memory unavailable, using templates only');\n      return base;\n    }\n  }\n  \n  async evolve(): Promise<void> {\n    // Evolution is enhancement, not core functionality\n    // If it fails, system continues with current behavior\n    try {\n      await this.evolutionCycle.run();\n    } catch (e) {\n      logger.error('Evolution failed, will retry next cycle', e);\n      // System continues unaffected\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\n**Degradation levels:**\n1. **Full health:** Neuro-memory + templates + evolution all working\n2. **Partial:** Neuro-memory slow/failing → templates only, evolution paused\n3. **Minimal:** Neuro-memory dead → templates only, no learning\n4. **Survival:** Even templates broken → hardcoded safe defaults\n\n**User impact:**\n- Level 1: Best experience, personalized\n- Level 2: Good experience, slightly generic\n- Level 3: Functional but obvious degradation\n- Level 4: System still usable, just dumb\n\n---\n\n## Bottom Line\n\n**Most critical risk:** Python crashes causing event mesh death.  \n**Most likely pain:** Conflicting patterns between neuro and templates.  \n**Best ROI fix:** Timeout + fallback on every neuro-memory call.\n\nThe architecture is sound IF you build it with failure in mind. Plan for neuro-memory to be wrong, slow, or dead - and design the rest of the system to carry on anyway."}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"zhipu","model":"glm-5","usage":{"input":2928,"output":3022,"cacheRead":11264,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":17214,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1773008246341}}
